le="font-size: 1pt;">&#8194;</div></td><td style="height: 1pt; width: 4.67pt; background-color: #C5C4CF;"><div style="font-size: 1pt;">&#8194;</div></td><td style="height: 1pt; width: 4.67pt; background-color: #C5C4CF;"><div style="font-size: 1pt;">&#8194;</div></td><td style="height: 1pt; width: 36pt; background-color: #C5C4CF;"><div style="font-size: 1pt;">&#8194;</div></td><td style="height: 1pt; width: 4pt; background-color: #C5C4CF;"><div style="font-size: 1pt;">&#8194;</div></td></tr></table><table border="0" cellpadding="0" style="border-spacing: 0; margin-top: 12pt; margin-left: 0pt;"><tr><td style="width: 24pt; text-align: left; vertical-align: top;"><div style="color: #000000; font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif; font-size: 10pt;">(1)<br/></div></td><td style="vertical-align: top;"><div style="color: #000000; font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; text-align: left;">Represents actual base salary earned by each named executive officer during the applicable year. </div></td></tr></table><table border="0" cellpadding="0" style="border-spacing: 0; margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 0pt;"><tr><td style="width: 24pt; text-align: left; vertical-align: top;"><div style="color: #000000; font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif; font-size: 10pt;">(2)<br/></div></td><td style="vertical-align: top;"><div style="color: #000000; font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; text-align: left;">Amounts shown do not reflect compensation actually received by the named executive officer. For each year, represents the grant date fair value of performance-based and service-based LTIP unit awards. The grant date fair value was determined in accordance with ASC Topic 718, disregarding for this purpose the estimate of forfeitures related to service-based vesting conditions. The maximum values of the 2024 performance-based LTIP units awards, assuming that the highest level of performance is achieved, are as follows: Mr. Crate-$1,033,565; Ms. Marino-$150,136; Mr. Ibe-$633,132; Mr. Logan-$66,534; and Ms.&#160;Baivier-$500,496. A discussion of the assumptions used in calculating these values can be found in Note 9 to our audited financial statements beginning on page F-26 of our Annual Report on Form 10-K for the year ended December&#160;31, 2024. </div></td></tr></table><table border="0" cellpadding="0" style="border-spacing: 0; margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 0pt;"><tr><td style="width: 24pt; text-align: left; vertical-align: top;"><div style="color: #000000; font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif; font-size: 10pt;">(3)<br/></div></td><td style="vertical-align: top;"><div style="color: #000000; font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; text-align: left;">For 2024, represents matching 401(k) plan contributions for each named executive officer, $500 matching contributions made by the Company to Mr. Crate and Ms. Marino and $250 to Mr. Logan, in each case pursuant to the Company's charitable donation-matching program. </div></td></tr></table></div></div><div class="BRDSX_block-frill" style="width: 468pt; margin-top: 12pt; margin-left: 0pt;"><div class="BRDSX_unknown" style="color: #000000; font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 9.47pt; text-align: center;">46<br/></div></div></div><div>
